; ted-freeonly-allocnull-dangling (#1006): DELETE LINE on the only line
; of the text (deleteline -> freelast -> freeonly) frees the line and
; then makes the new empty line with allocfirst, whose afirst2 ignores a
; failed allocnull: firstitem, enditem and thisitem point at the freed
; line.  TED alone under inject (alerts answered): one line "a", DELETE
; LINE; the 4th AllocMem of 10 bytes (MEMF_PUBLIC) of TED's process,
; that allocnull, fails (the first three are made at the start).  SAVE,
; QUIT.
; Correct (the fix of the issue): the alert "Not enough memory for
; operation!", the line stays and is saved as it is; the original saves
; what the freed memory holds then (or crashes).
; @fixed #1006
; @file bo.bas "a"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts allocfail=10-10/f=1/1+3 blitz2:ted @FILE@
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 1 allocations failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: alert: Not enough memory for operation!"
; @expect data bo.bas "a\n"
timeout 20
wait screen
menu 1 6
wait screen
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
